<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salvadoran Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1979">1979</a>–<a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Salvadoran Civil War was fought from 1979 to 1992 between the military-led government of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti-national-liberation-front">Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front</a>, a coalition of left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> groups. More than 75,000 people died, many in massacres of civilians such as El Mozote. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chapultepec-peace-accords">Chapultepec Peace Accords</a> of 1992 ended the war and turned the FMLN into a political party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salvadoran-civil-war.jpg" alt="Salvadoran Civil War" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Images compiled by PizzaKing13 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salvadoran_Civil_War_image_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
